{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>If you afflict my daughters.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said its meaning is: if you do not lie with your wives. This is a foreign expression; nothing like it is heard in all of Scripture. And if it were according to its plain meaning, what harm is there? The meaning is that he not do evil to them and force them into something they do not desire. And the Targum of Gilead: Yegar Sahadutha."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:40.668714572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}